From 4a563d85ed9bbc625d46cd522206842648400e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:29:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: fade the parked tab sheet morph over the real bar when
 a close ends

The bottom tab sheet close slid down smoothly, then jumped in one
frame: the morph pill changed text, the extension icons appeared and
the glass window left. The close parked the morph on the bar, showed the
real bar under it for a single frame, and then removed the morph, its
icon copies and the cover while they were still opaque. The real icons
stayed hidden until that last frame, and the real url text is laid out
differently from the morph text (it is cut short by the extension
icons), so that last frame changed every one of them at once.

The reveal frame now starts a short timed fade, scaled by the animator
duration scale. The real icons are shown again at the reveal, under the
cover and the icon copies. The morph and the icon copies fade out over
the whole fade, and the cover clears over the first part of it, so the
real bar comes through as a cross-fade. The last frame only removes
views that are already clear. Opening the sheet again during the fade
puts the morph back to opaque. With animations off the old two-frame
hand-off is kept.

The open path, the spring, the button bar slide and the pull from the
button bar are unchanged. The unit tests cover the fade and a reopen
during it.
